---
import CalculatorLayout from '../../layouts/CalculatorLayout.astro';
---

<CalculatorLayout
  title="Compound Interest Calculator – Calculate Investment Growth"
  description="Calculate compound interest and estimate how your money may grow over time based on your initial investment, interest rate, duration, compounding frequency, and optional regular contributions."
  category="Finance"
  calculatorName="Compound Interest Calculator"
  slug="compound-interest-calculator"
  keywords={[
    'compound interest calculator',
    'daily compound interest calculator',
    'monthly compound interest calculator',
    'compound interest calculator india'
  ]}
>
  <div class="space-y-6">

    <!-- QUICK PRESETS BAR -->
    <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200/90 bg-white p-3.5 shadow-2xs dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-1.5 text-xs">
        <span class="font-bold text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 mr-1 flex items-center gap-1">
          <span>⚡</span> Quick Examples:
        </span>
        <button type="button" class="btn-ci-preset rounded-lg border border-slate-300 bg-white px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-blue-500 hover:text-blue-600 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 cursor-pointer" data-p="100000" data-r="10" data-t="10" data-u="years" data-f="annually" data-c="0">📈 Long-Term (₹1L @ 10%, 10 Yrs, Annual)</button>
        <button type="button" class="btn-ci-preset rounded-lg border border-slate-300 bg-white px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-blue-500 hover:text-blue-600 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 cursor-pointer" data-p="50000" data-r="8" data-t="5" data-u="years" data-f="monthly" data-c="0">📅 Monthly Compounding (₹50k @ 8%, 5 Yrs)</button>
        <button type="button" class="btn-ci-preset rounded-lg border border-slate-300 bg-white px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-blue-500 hover:text-blue-600 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 cursor-pointer" data-p="100000" data-r="7" data-t="3" data-u="years" data-f="daily" data-c="0">⚡ Daily Compounding (₹1L @ 7%, 3 Yrs)</button>
        <button type="button" class="btn-ci-preset rounded-lg border border-slate-300 bg-white px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-blue-500 hover:text-blue-600 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 cursor-pointer" data-p="100000" data-r="12" data-t="10" data-u="years" data-f="monthly" data-c="5000" data-cf="monthly" data-ct="end">💰 Regular SIP (₹1L + ₹5k/mo @ 12%)</button>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- MAIN CALCULATOR FORM CONTAINER -->
    <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-3xl border border-slate-200/90 bg-linear-to-br from-white via-slate-50 to-blue-50/30 p-5 shadow-xl shadow-slate-900/5 dark:border-slate-800 dark:from-slate-950 dark:via-slate-950 dark:to-blue-950/20 sm:p-7">
      
      <div class="border-b border-slate-200/80 pb-3 dark:border-slate-800">
        <h2 class="text-base sm:text-lg font-black tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-2">
          <span>📊</span> Compound Interest Calculator
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
          Calculate compound interest and estimate how your money may grow over time based on your initial investment, interest rate, duration, compounding frequency, and optional regular contributions.
        </p>
      </div>

      <form id="form-ci" class="mt-4 space-y-4" novalidate onsubmit="return false;">
        
        <!-- ROW 1: PRIMARY INVESTMENT DETAILS -->
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-3 sm:grid-cols-4">
          <!-- Initial Investment -->
          <div>
            <label for="inp-ci-principal" class="block text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">Initial Principal (₹)</label>
            <input type="number" id="inp-ci-principal" value="100000" step="10000" min="0" class="mt-1.5 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white p-2.5 text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-white" placeholder="1,00,000" />
          </div>

          <!-- Annual Interest Rate -->
          <div>
            <label for="inp-ci-rate" class="block text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">Annual Return Rate (%)</label>
            <input type="number" id="inp-ci-rate" value="10" step="0.5" min="0" max="100" class="mt-1.5 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white p-2.5 text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-white" placeholder="10" />
          </div>

          <!-- Duration & Unit -->
          <div>
            <label for="inp-ci-duration" class="block text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">Duration</label>
            <div class="mt-1.5 flex rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800">
              <input type="number" id="inp-ci-duration" value="10" step="1" min="1" max="100" class="w-full rounded-l-xl border-0 p-2.5 text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 focus:ring-0 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-white" placeholder="10" />
              <select id="sel-ci-dur-unit" class="rounded-r-xl border-l border-slate-300 bg-slate-50 px-2.5 text-xs font-bold text-slate-700 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-900 dark:text-slate-300 cursor-pointer">
                <option value="years" selected>Years</option>
                <option value="months">Months</option>
              </select>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Compounding Frequency -->
          <div>
            <label for="sel-ci-freq" class="block text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">Compounding Frequency</label>
            <select id="sel-ci-freq" class="mt-1.5 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white p-2.5 text-sm font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-white cursor-pointer">
              <option value="annually" selected>Annually (1/yr)</option>
              <option value="quarterly">Quarterly (4/yr)</option>
              <option value="monthly">Monthly (12/yr)</option>
              <option value="daily">Daily (365/yr)</option>
            </select>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- ROW 2: OPTIONAL REGULAR CONTRIBUTIONS -->
        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-blue-200 bg-blue-50/30 p-4 dark:border-blue-900/60 dark:bg-blue-950/20 space-y-3">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
            <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-blue-700 dark:text-blue-300 flex items-center gap-1.5">
              <span>➕</span> Optional Regular Contributions
            </span>
            <span class="text-[11px] font-semibold text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">Leave at 0 if none</span>
          </div>

          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-3 sm:grid-cols-3">
            <div>
              <label for="inp-ci-contrib" class="block text-xs font-bold text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">Contribution Amount (₹)</label>
              <input type="number" id="inp-ci-contrib" value="0" step="500" min="0" class="mt-1.5 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white p-2 text-xs font-bold dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-white" placeholder="0" />
            </div>

            <div>
              <label for="sel-ci-contrib-freq" class="block text-xs font-bold text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">Contribution Frequency</label>
              <select id="sel-ci-contrib-freq" class="mt-1.5 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white p-2 text-xs font-semibold dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-white cursor-pointer">
                <option value="monthly" selected>Monthly</option>
                <option value="yearly">Yearly</option>
              </select>
            </div>

            <div>
              <label for="sel-ci-contrib-timing" class="block text-xs font-bold text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">Contribution Timing</label>
              <select id="sel-ci-contrib-timing" class="mt-1.5 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white p-2 text-xs font-semibold dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-white cursor-pointer">
                <option value="end" selected>End of Period</option>
                <option value="beginning">Beginning of Period</option>
              </select>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 pt-2">
          <button type="submit" id="btn-calc-ci" class="flex-1 rounded-xl bg-blue-600 hover:bg-blue-700 px-6 py-3 text-sm font-extrabold text-white shadow-lg shadow-blue-600/25 transition active:scale-[0.98] cursor-pointer">
            Calculate Compound Interest →
          </button>
          <button type="button" id="btn-clear-ci" class="rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white px-4 py-3 text-sm font-bold text-slate-700 hover:bg-slate-100 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 transition cursor-pointer">
            Clear All (✕)
          </button>
        </div>

        <p id="err-ci" class="hidden rounded-xl border border-red-200 bg-red-50 p-2.5 text-xs font-semibold text-red-700 dark:border-red-900/60 dark:bg-red-950/30 dark:text-red-300" role="alert" aria-live="polite"></p>

      </form>

      <!-- RESULTS PRESENTATION SECTION (Hidden Initially) -->
      <div id="ci-results-section" class="hidden mt-6 space-y-5">
        
        <!-- Main Highlight Card -->
        <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-3xl border border-emerald-200 bg-linear-to-br from-white via-emerald-50/40 to-emerald-100/50 p-5 shadow-lg shadow-emerald-500/5 dark:border-emerald-900/60 dark:from-slate-950 dark:via-slate-900 dark:to-emerald-950/30 sm:p-7">
          <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:justify-between gap-4 border-b border-emerald-200/80 pb-4 dark:border-slate-800">
            <div>
              <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-300">Estimated Future Value</span>
              <div id="res-ci-future-val" class="mt-1 text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-black text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400">₹ 2,59,374.25</div>
            </div>
            <div class="sm:text-right">
              <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">Total Interest Earned:</span>
              <div id="res-ci-total-interest" class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-black text-slate-900 dark:text-white">₹ 1,59,374.25</div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="mt-4 grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-4 gap-3 text-xs">
            <div class="rounded-xl border border-emerald-200/60 bg-white/80 p-3 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900/70">
              <div class="text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 font-semibold">Initial Investment</div>
              <div id="res-ci-initial" class="mt-1 text-sm sm:text-base font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">₹ 1,00,000</div>
            </div>
            <div class="rounded-xl border border-emerald-200/60 bg-white/80 p-3 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900/70">
              <div class="text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 font-semibold">Total Contributions</div>
              <div id="res-ci-contrib-total" class="mt-1 text-sm sm:text-base font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">₹ 0</div>
            </div>
            <div class="rounded-xl border border-emerald-200/60 bg-white/80 p-3 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900/70">
              <div class="text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 font-semibold">Total Principal Invested</div>
              <div id="res-ci-total-invested" class="mt-1 text-sm sm:text-base font-bold text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400">₹ 1,00,000</div>
            </div>
            <div class="rounded-xl border border-emerald-200/60 bg-white/80 p-3 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900/70">
              <div class="text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 font-semibold">Doubling Time (Rule 72)</div>
              <div id="res-ci-rule72" class="mt-1 text-sm sm:text-base font-bold text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400">7.2 Years</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- GROWTH BREAKDOWN CARD & CHART -->
        <div class="rounded-3xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900 space-y-4">
          <h3 class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 flex items-center gap-1.5">
            <span>📈</span> Investment Growth & Portfolio Ratio
          </h3>

          <!-- Visual Ratio Bar Chart -->
          <div class="space-y-2">
            <div class="h-4 w-full overflow-hidden rounded-full bg-slate-100 flex dark:bg-slate-800">
              <div id="bar-ci-principal" class="bg-blue-600 transition-all duration-500" style="width: 38.5%;" title="Principal Deposited"></div>
              <div id="bar-ci-interest" class="bg-emerald-500 transition-all duration-500" style="width: 61.5%;" title="Interest Accrued"></div>
            </div>
            <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between text-xs font-semibold text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
              <span class="flex items-center gap-1.5">
                <span class="inline-block h-3 w-3 rounded-full bg-blue-600"></span>
                <span id="lbl-chart-principal">Principal Invested: ₹1,00,000 (38.5%)</span>
              </span>
              <span class="flex items-center gap-1.5">
                <span class="inline-block h-3 w-3 rounded-full bg-emerald-500"></span>
                <span id="lbl-chart-interest">Compound Interest: ₹1,59,374 (61.5%)</span>
              </span>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Detailed Calculation Explanation -->
          <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200/80 bg-slate-50/70 p-4 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-950/60 space-y-1 text-xs">
            <div class="font-bold text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200">How Your Compound Interest Was Calculated:</div>
            <div class="font-mono text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400" id="txt-ci-explanation">
              Initial principal of ₹1,00,000 compounded annually at 10.0% p.a. across 10 years (10 compounding cycles).
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- INVESTMENT GROWTH SCHEDULE (YEARLY & MONTHLY TABS) -->
        <div class="rounded-3xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900">
          <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:justify-between gap-3 mb-4">
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 flex items-center gap-1.5">
                <span>📅</span> Investment Growth Schedule
              </h3>
              <p class="text-[11px] text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">
                View yearly or month-by-month compound interest accumulation.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
              <!-- View Switcher Tabs -->
              <div class="inline-flex rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-100 p-1 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 text-xs font-bold">
                <button type="button" id="tab-ci-yearly" class="active rounded-lg bg-white px-3 py-1 text-slate-900 shadow-xs dark:bg-slate-900 dark:text-white cursor-pointer">
                  Yearly Summary
                </button>
                <button type="button" id="tab-ci-monthly" class="rounded-lg px-3 py-1 text-slate-600 hover:text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-400 dark:hover:text-white cursor-pointer">
                  Monthly Schedule
                </button>
              </div>

              <!-- Download PDF Button -->
              <button type="button" id="btn-ci-download-pdf" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-xl bg-emerald-600 hover:bg-emerald-700 px-3.5 py-1.5 text-xs font-bold text-white shadow-xs transition active:scale-[0.98] cursor-pointer" title="Download active schedule as PDF">
                <span>📄</span> <span id="txt-btn-ci-pdf">Download PDF</span>
              </button>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Schedule Table Container -->
          <div class="overflow-x-auto max-h-96 scrollbar-thin">
            <table class="w-full text-left text-xs">
              <thead id="ci-sched-thead" class="bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 font-bold sticky top-0">
                <!-- Injected dynamically -->
              </thead>
              <tbody id="ci-sched-tbody" class="divide-y divide-slate-100 dark:divide-slate-800 font-mono">
                <!-- Injected dynamically -->
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>

    </div>

  </div>

  <!-- EDUCATIONAL SEO ARTICLE SLOT (Styled matching age.astro) -->
  <Fragment slot="content">
    <section class="ci-content">
      <h2>How to Use This Compound Interest Calculator</h2>
      <p>
        Planning your financial growth is straightforward with this multi-frequency compounding engine:
      </p>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Enter your initial investment:</strong> Input the starting lump-sum deposit in Indian Rupees (₹).</li>
        <li><strong>Enter the expected annual rate:</strong> Input your anticipated interest or return rate percentage (e.g. 10% per annum).</li>
        <li><strong>Select investment duration:</strong> Enter the timeframe and choose whether it is in <em>Years</em> or <em>Months</em>.</li>
        <li><strong>Choose compounding frequency:</strong> Select <em>Annually</em>, <em>Quarterly</em>, <em>Monthly</em>, or <em>Daily</em> (assumes 365 days/year).</li>
        <li><strong>Add optional regular contributions:</strong> Enter monthly or yearly additions, and select whether deposits occur at the beginning or end of each period.</li>
        <li><strong>Click Calculate Compound Interest:</strong> Instantly view the estimated future maturity value and cumulative interest.</li>
        <li><strong>Examine the growth ratio bar:</strong> See the percentage split between your deposited principal and interest earned.</li>
        <li><strong>Explore growth schedules:</strong> Toggle between the <em>Yearly Summary</em> and <em>Monthly Schedule</em>.</li>
        <li><strong>Download PDF:</strong> Export your active schedule as a professional PDF report with website branding.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2>Compound Interest Calculation Example</h2>
      <p>
        Consider an initial investment of <strong>₹1,00,000</strong> invested at an annual return rate of <strong>10%</strong> for <strong>10 years</strong> with annual compounding ($n = 1$):
      </p>
      <div class="my-4 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-4 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900 text-xs sm:text-sm space-y-1.5 font-mono">
        <div>Principal (P) = ₹1,00,000</div>
        <div>Annual Rate (r) = 10% (0.10)</div>
        <div>Compounding Frequency (n) = 1 (Annual)</div>
        <div>Time (t) = 10 Years</div>
        <div>Future Value = ₹1,00,000 × (1 + 0.10/1)^(1 × 10) = <strong>₹2,59,374.25</strong></div>
        <div class="text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400 font-bold">Total Interest Earned = ₹2,59,374.25 − ₹1,00,000 = ₹1,59,374.25</div>
      </div>
      <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 italic">
        * This is an illustrative estimate. Actual investment returns may fluctuate based on market conditions, taxation, and fees.
      </p>

      <h2>Daily vs Monthly Compounding</h2>
      <p>
        The frequency at which interest is calculated and added back to your principal affects the effective annual yield:
      </p>

      <div class="overflow-x-auto my-4">
        <table class="w-full text-left text-xs sm:text-sm border-collapse border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">
          <thead class="bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 text-slate-900 dark:text-white font-bold">
            <tr>
              <th class="p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Compounding Frequency</th>
              <th class="p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Periods Per Year (n)</th>
              <th class="p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Growth on ₹1 Lakh @ 10% (10 Yrs)</th>
              <th class="p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Effective Annual Rate</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-200 dark:divide-slate-800 text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
            <tr>
              <td class="p-3 font-semibold border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Annually</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">1</td>
              <td class="p-3 font-mono border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">₹2,59,374.25</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">10.00%</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-3 font-semibold border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Quarterly</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">4</td>
              <td class="p-3 font-mono border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">₹2,68,506.38</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">10.38%</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-3 font-semibold border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Monthly</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">12</td>
              <td class="p-3 font-mono border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">₹2,70,704.15</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">10.47%</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-3 font-semibold border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Daily (365 days)</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">365</td>
              <td class="p-3 font-mono border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">₹2,71,790.96</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">10.52%</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h2>Compound Interest vs Simple Interest</h2>
      <p>
        Understanding how compounding accelerates returns compared to simple interest is fundamental to long-term wealth planning:
      </p>

      <div class="overflow-x-auto my-4">
        <table class="w-full text-left text-xs sm:text-sm border-collapse border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">
          <thead class="bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 text-slate-900 dark:text-white font-bold">
            <tr>
              <th class="p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Factor</th>
              <th class="p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Simple Interest</th>
              <th class="p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Compound Interest</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-200 dark:divide-slate-800 text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
            <tr>
              <td class="p-3 font-semibold border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Interest Base</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Applied only to the initial principal deposit</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Applied to principal + all previously accumulated interest</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-3 font-semibold border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Growth Over Time</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Linear (constant fixed returns each year)</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Exponential (returns accelerate as balance grows)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-3 font-semibold border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Long Duration Effect</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Produces steady, predictable yield</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Dramatically outpaces simple interest over 10+ years</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-3 font-semibold border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Common Applications</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Short-term loans, basic debt instruments</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Mutual funds, stocks, PPF, EPF, fixed deposits</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h2>How Compounding Can Affect Long-Term Growth</h2>
      <p>
        The power of compounding relies on key behavioral habits:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Starting Early:</strong> Time is the most potent multiplier in compounding. Investing small amounts in your twenties often yields more than investing larger sums starting in your forties.</li>
        <li><strong>Staying Invested Longer:</strong> Over longer periods, compounding can have a greater effect because returns may themselves begin generating additional returns.</li>
        <li><strong>Making Regular Contributions:</strong> Adding regular monthly or annual contributions consistently replenishes the capital base being compounded.</li>
        <li><strong>Reinvesting Returns:</strong> Reinvesting dividends and interest payouts rather than withdrawing them preserves the compounding loop.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Compound Interest Calculator for Indian Investors</h2>
      <p>
        This calculator defaults to Indian Rupee (₹) formatting and Indian numerical standards (e.g. <strong>₹1,00,000</strong> for 1 Lakh, <strong>₹10,00,000</strong> for 10 Lakhs, and <strong>₹1,00,00,000</strong> for 1 Crore). In India, instruments like Public Provident Fund (PPF) compound annually, fixed deposits often compound quarterly, and mutual fund SIPs compound continuously with market NAV appreciation.
      </p>

      <h2>Common Mistakes When Using a Compound Interest Calculator</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Confusing Interest Rate with Guaranteed Return:</strong> Equity and mutual fund returns are variable market projections, not fixed guaranteed yields.</li>
        <li><strong>Selecting the Wrong Compounding Frequency:</strong> Assuming an annual compounding bank deposit is compounding daily or vice versa.</li>
        <li><strong>Ignoring Regular Contributions:</strong> Forgetting to account for monthly SIP additions which represent significant wealth creation.</li>
        <li><strong>Confusing Simple and Compound Interest:</strong> Treating compounding calculations as basic linear multipliers.</li>
        <li><strong>Overlooking Taxes and Inflation:</strong> Capital gains tax (LTCG/STCG) and purchasing power inflation reduce real net returns.</li>
        <li><strong>Ignoring Expense Ratios & Fees:</strong> Fund management fees and exit loads can reduce net compounded yields over time.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Important Assumptions and Information</h2>
      <p>
        Please review these key principles:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Constant Rate Assumption:</strong> Calculations assume a steady annual percentage return throughout the selected duration.</li>
        <li><strong>Day-Count Convention:</strong> Daily compounding calculations assume a standard 365-day Gregorian calendar year.</li>
        <li><strong>Educational Estimates:</strong> This tool provides mathematical simulations and does not offer certified investment, tax, or legal advice.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </Fragment>

  <!-- FAQ SECTION SLOT (EXACTLY 7 FAQs AS REQUIRED) -->
  <Fragment slot="faq">
    <div class="space-y-4 text-xs sm:text-sm">
      
      <details class="group rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-4 dark:border-slate-800" open>
        <summary class="cursor-pointer list-none">
          <h3 class="flex items-center justify-between font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
            1. How does a compound interest calculator work?
            <span class="group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">▼</span>
          </h3>
        </summary>
        <p class="mt-2 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
          A compound interest calculator models how an initial investment and optional regular contributions grow over time by adding accrued interest back to the principal at chosen compounding intervals (annually, quarterly, monthly, or daily).
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="group rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-4 dark:border-slate-800">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer list-none">
          <h3 class="flex items-center justify-between font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
            2. What is the formula for compound interest?
            <span class="group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">▼</span>
          </h3>
        </summary>
        <p class="mt-2 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
          The formula for a lump sum is <code>A = P × (1 + r/n)^(n × t)</code>, where <em>A</em> is future value, <em>P</em> is initial principal, <em>r</em> is annual interest rate (decimal), <em>n</em> is compounding frequency per year, and <em>t</em> is time in years.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="group rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-4 dark:border-slate-800">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer list-none">
          <h3 class="flex items-center justify-between font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
            3. How is daily compound interest calculated?
            <span class="group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">▼</span>
          </h3>
        </summary>
        <p class="mt-2 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
          Daily compound interest uses <code>n = 365</code> compounding periods per year. The formula becomes: <code>A = P × (1 + r/365)^(365 × t)</code>.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="group rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-4 dark:border-slate-800">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer list-none">
          <h3 class="flex items-center justify-between font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
            4. How does monthly compounding work?
            <span class="group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">▼</span>
          </h3>
        </summary>
        <p class="mt-2 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
          In monthly compounding, interest is calculated and added to the principal 12 times per year (<code>n = 12</code>). Each month's interest is based on the updated balance from the previous month.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="group rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-4 dark:border-slate-800">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer list-none">
          <h3 class="flex items-center justify-between font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
            5. What is the difference between simple and compound interest?
            <span class="group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">▼</span>
          </h3>
        </summary>
        <p class="mt-2 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
          Simple interest earns a fixed return strictly on the original principal deposit. Compound interest earns returns on both the principal and all accumulated interest from previous periods, leading to exponential growth.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="group rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-4 dark:border-slate-800">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer list-none">
          <h3 class="flex items-center justify-between font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
            6. Can I add regular monthly contributions to the calculator?
            <span class="group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">▼</span>
          </h3>
        </summary>
        <p class="mt-2 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
          Yes. You can enter an optional monthly or yearly contribution and choose whether deposits occur at the beginning or end of each period for exact growth modeling.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="group rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-4 dark:border-slate-800">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer list-none">
          <h3 class="flex items-center justify-between font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
            7. Is the compound interest result guaranteed?
            <span class="group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">▼</span>
          </h3>
        </summary>
        <p class="mt-2 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
          The calculator provides mathematical estimates based on a steady rate of return. Actual outcomes on market investments (mutual funds, stocks) vary, whereas fixed deposits and government savings schemes offer predetermined rates.
        </p>
      </details>

    </div>
  </Fragment>
</CalculatorLayout>

